66d889f",30,-11,0,"Would there ever be a content x offset?"],["c239a6bb_7e2f5bff",30,-11,1,"nit: bottom"],["65d84343_4f26dda7",31,-7,1,"Nit: can you update the param name of this as well? I know this will eventually go away so it seems a bit moot but may as well for consistency."],["e12faeea_a0fe2536",31,-7,1,"Nit: this wording of this @return javadoc seems a bit odd to me. Is there a reason this was updated?"],["77d01086_4e5bf9b2",37,-6,0,"Just breaking out a comment from the other thread: What does focus_rect mean/return here? Does it cover the entire focus node? Is that a problem e.g. if the focus node itself is large (like a…"],["a5c3aafb_9262f278",39,-6,1,"Sorry to keep adjusting the naming: if this flag covers both text cursor and input focus, you could also just have this as `sAccessibilityMagnificationFollowsFocus`, since \"input focus\" often means…"],["56016ec4_de214b91",37,-4,1,"What impact do these have? What if we're in a rtl language? Will we get the wrong side of the selection? Likely worth a quick test."],["9f4dae7d_fd8f79df",30,-4,1,"nit/optional: fromCssToDevicePix"],["a25e9aeb_e28c0180",30,-4,0,"Is there any AndroidX support for this type of fallback? (or any AndroidX support at all)?"],["b6a018f4_77027cf7",31,-4,0,"Just curious, but I would think this naming discrepancy would have been caught by a linter?"]],0,25],[7170338,20419,179,4.338,3.354,[[9,0.487,7,90],[10,0.251,3,47],[11,0.115,3,20],[12,0.073,5,12],[15,0.031,1,4],[16,0.021,2,3],[14,0.021,2,3]],[["eef9ab11_05338a85",30,-2,1,"One of these cases is when delegate.requestInputFocusOnScreen return false, right? Does that case occur for any other reason? Also, I don't know what source-tagged means. Is that commonly used…"],["3cced51e_193e7952",30,0,1,"optional if possible: This is a private bug. Could you please open it, and/or reference a new one? See [Chromium Issue Tracker Guidelines for Google…"]],0,26],[7150380,20424,137,4.338,3.354,[[9,0.815,8,116],[20,0.116,2,16],[21,0.055,1,6],[12,0.014,6,1]],[],0,27],[7232651,20433,8,0.406,0.291,[[25,0.455,1,4],[9,0.273,9,2],[11,0.273,4,2]],[],0,28],[7261737,20439,33,0.729,0.57,[[27,0.864,0,28],[28,0.136,0,5]],[],0,29],[7270406,20441,91,1.637,1.223,[[24,2]],[["6b07c4ac_d79c9b63",40,0,1,"```suggestion Vector<gfx::Rect> expected = {gfx::Rect(0, 0, 40, 10)}; ```"],["e23ec5d7_a412529d",40,0,1,"I would just add the gmock include and do: ```suggestion EXPECT_THAT(expected, ContainerEq(actual)); ``` (This will need a using `::testing::ContainerEq` somewhere as well)"]],0,30]]}